        <article class="entry" id="l01" data-n="01" data-title="The Mouse & the Mill" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false">
          <div class="e-head"><span class="e-num mono">No. 01</span><span class="e-leader"></span><h3 class="e-title">The Mouse &amp; the Mill</h3></div>
          <div class="stamp e-stamp" aria-hidden="true">APPROVED</div>
          <div class="stamp e-heard" aria-hidden="true">SECOND HEARING</div>
          <p class="verse">
            <span class="la">There once was a fellow named Bill</span>
            <span class="la">Whose factory hummed like a mill.</span>
            <span class="lb">A mouse nibbled wires;</span>
            <span class="lb">The looms spun up the stairs;</span>
            <span class="la">And the town still smells like a mill.</span>
          </p>
          <footer class="e-foot"><span>Ref. BL-01</span><span>filed: mills</span><span class="f-lead"></span><span>rhyme: mill</span><span class="price">1 giggle</span></footer>
        </article>

        <article class="entry" id="l02" data-n="02" data-title="The Great Loaf" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false">
          <div class="e-head"><span class="e-num mono">No. 02</span><span class="e-leader"></span><h3 class="e-title">The Great Loaf</h3></div>
          <div class="stamp e-stamp" aria-hidden="true">APPROVED</div>
          <div class="stamp e-heard" aria-hidden="true">SECOND HEARING</div>
          <p class="verse">
            <span class="la">A baker named Bill, stout as a wall,</span>
            <span class="la">Raised a loaf the size of a ball.</span>
            <span class="lb">He offered it to a mule;</span>
            <span class="lb">The mule ate the whole —</span>
            <span class="la">He ate the whole thing and all.</span>
          </p>
          <footer class="e-foot"><span>Ref. BL-02</span><span>filed: ovens</span><span class="f-lead"></span><span>rhyme: all</span><span class="price">1 giggle</span></footer>
        </article>

        <article class="entry" id="l03" data-n="03" data-title="The Economist" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false">
          <div class="e-head"><span class="e-num mono">No. 03</span><span class="e-leader"></span><h3 class="e-title">The Economist</h3><span class="tag">† the economist</span></div>
          <div class="stamp e-stamp" aria-hidden="true">APPROVED</div>
          <div class="stamp e-heard" aria-hidden="true">SECOND HEARING</div>
          <p class="verse">
            <span class="la">An economist named Bill, quite a swell,</span>
            <span class="la">Swore that prices would climb like a swell.</span>
            <span class="lb">He bought with his last,</span>
            <span class="lb">of his savings, alas —</span>
            <span class="la">Then the market fell down, and that was the spell.</span>
          </p>
          <footer class="e-foot"><span>Ref. BL-03</span><span>filed: markets</span><span class="f-lead"></span><span>rhyme: spell</span><span class="price">1 giggle</span></footer>
        </article>

        <article class="entry" id="l04" data-n="04" data-title="The Jurgen from Hamburg" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false">
          <div class="e-head"><span class="e-num mono">No. 04</span><span class="e-leader"></span><h3 class="e-title">The Jurgen from Hamburg</h3><span class="tag">† the jurgen</span></div>
          <div class="stamp e-stamp" aria-hidden="true">APPROVED</div>
          <div class="stamp e-heard" aria-hidden="true">SECOND HEARING</div>
          <p class="verse">
            <span class="la">A Jurgen from Hamburg, named Schmitt,</span>
            <span class="la">Told Bill, “Your economy's fit</span>
            <span class="lb">For a coat of old flannel.”</span>
            <span class="lb">Bill wore it, quite manly,</span>
            <span class="la">And the Jurgen departed in triumph, still.</span>
          </p>
          <footer class="e-foot"><span>Ref. BL-04</span><span>filed: hamburg</span><span class="f-lead"></span><span>rhyme: still</span><span class="price">1 giggle</span></footer>
        </article>

        <article class="entry" id="l05" data-n="05" data-title="Kettle for the Bull" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false">
          <div class="e-head"><span class="e-num mono">No. 05</span><span class="e-leader"></span><h3 class="e-title">Kettle for the Bull</h3></div>
          <div class="stamp e-stamp" aria-hidden="true">APPROVED</div>
          <div class="stamp e-heard" aria-hidden="true">SECOND HEARING</div>
          <p class="verse">
            <span class="la">A butcher named Bill fed his bull</span>
            <span class="la">A whole kettle of stew and a bowl.</span>
            <span class="lb">The bull huffed and puffed,</span>
            <span class="lb">Then he licked up the fluff —</span>
            <span class="la">And he rumbled and rumbled, full.</span>
          </p>
          <footer class="e-foot"><span>Ref. BL-05</span><span>filed: livestock</span><span class="f-lead"></span><span>rhyme: full</span><span class="price">1 giggle</span></footer>
        </article>

        <article class="entry" id="l06" data-n="06" data-title="The Bell of the Hall" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false">
          <div class="e-head"><span class="e-num mono">No. 06</span><span class="e-leader"></span><h3 class="e-title">The Bell of the Hall</h3></div>
          <div class="stamp e-stamp" aria-hidden="true">APPROVED</div>
          <div class="stamp e-heard" aria-hidden="true">SECOND HEARING</div>
          <p class="verse">
            <span class="la">Young Bill rang the bell of the hall</span>
            <span class="la">Till the bell got a crack and it fell</span>
            <span class="lb">Into Bill's pie tin,</span>
            <span class="lb">And the town, in its din,</span>
            <span class="la">Named a new bell after him — “Bill.”</span>
          </p>
          <footer class="e-foot"><span>Ref. BL-06</span><span>filed: bells</span><span class="f-lead"></span><span>rhyme: bill</span><span class="price">1 giggle</span></footer>
        </article>

        <article class="entry" id="l07" data-n="07" data-title="The Growing Bill" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false">
          <div class="e-head"><span class="e-num mono">No. 07</span><span class="e-leader"></span><h3 class="e-title">The Growing Bill</h3></div>
          <div class="stamp e-stamp" aria-hidden="true">APPROVED</div>
          <div class="stamp e-heard" aria-hidden="true">SECOND HEARING</div>
          <p class="verse">
            <span class="la">Old Bill got a bill, and it grew,</span>
            <span class="la">Till the total was a number too round</span>
            <span class="lb">For a single old man to pay;</span>
            <span class="lb">So he paid half in hay</span>
            <span class="la">And the rest in a hug — and that was sound.</span>
          </p>
          <footer class="e-foot"><span>Ref. BL-07</span><span>filed: debts</span><span class="f-lead"></span><span>rhyme: sound</span><span class="price">1 giggle</span></footer>
        </article>

        <article class="entry" id="l08" data-n="08" data-title="Off by a Bull" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false">
          <div class="e-head"><span class="e-num mono">No. 08</span><span class="e-leader"></span><h3 class="e-title">Off by a Bull</h3></div>
          <div class="stamp e-stamp" aria-hidden="true">APPROVED</div>
          <div class="stamp e-heard" aria-hidden="true">SECOND HEARING</div>
          <p class="verse">
            <span class="la">A farmer named Bill kept a bill</span>
            <span class="la">Of his cattle, all numbered and still.</span>
            <span class="lb">But the numbers were wrong —</span>
            <span class="lb">Every cow had moved along —</span>
            <span class="la">And the total was off by a bull.</span>
          </p>
          <footer class="e-foot"><span>Ref. BL-08</span><span>filed: livestock</span><span class="f-lead"></span><span>rhyme: bull</span><span class="price">1 giggle</span></footer>
        </article>

