        <article class="entry" id="l09" data-n="09" data-title="A List of Twenty-Five" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-pressed="false">
          <div class="e-head"><span class="e-num mono">No. 09</span><span class="e-leader"></span><h3 class="e-title">A List of Twenty-Five</h3></div>
          <div class="stamp e-stamp" aria-hidden="true">APPROVED</div>
          <div class="stamp e-heard" aria-hidden="true">SECOND HEARING</div>
          <p class="verse">
            <span class="la">A poet named Bill set his quill</span>
            <span class="la">To a list of the limericks he'd fill.</span>
            <span class="lb">Twenty-five, he said,</span>
            <span class="lb">for a fellow called —</span>
            <span class="la">And he signed off: “Best regards, Bill.”</span>
          </p>
          <footer class="e-foot"><span>Ref. BL-09</span><span>filed: poetry</span><span class="f-lead"></span><span>rhyme: bill</span><span class="price">1 giggle</span></footer>
        </article>

